From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] annot, ui-egui: added text and new text boxes start in Times
 12 pt; a text box keeps the font its /DA names

Owner decision 2026-10-29 (docs/phase4/design-system.md, "Revised"): text the user adds starts in Times New Roman 12 pt. In a PDF that is the standard-14 Times (Times-Roman, `/TiRo`): nothing is embedded, Windows viewers show Times New Roman and the renderer's own standard-font substitute draws it elsewhere. The Add Text tool's default style and new text boxes, typewriter text and callouts use it; a text box's appearance, rich text and refit now follow the font its /DA names, so a colour or size change keeps it and boxes already in a file keep their Helvetica (measured exactly as before).
---
